---

<Base
  title="Custom Home Builder in the Catalina Foothills, Tucson | Lathrem Homebuilders"
  description="Licensed custom home builder in the Catalina Foothills, Tucson. Hillside lots, Pima County ordinance experience, remodels and outdoor living. AZ ROC #324057, 5.0 across 19 reviews."
  canonical="/custom-home-builder-catalina-foothills.html"
  schema={schema}
>
  <!-- ================= PAGE HEAD ================= -->
  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Areas served</p>
      <h1 class="display h-xl">Custom home builder in the Catalina Foothills</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width:58ch;margin-top:26px">Hillside residences, remodels and outdoor living on the slopes above Tucson: Ventana Canyon, Skyline, Pima Canyon, Finger Rock and the streets off Sabino Canyon Road.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= LOCAL CONTEXT ================= -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--top">
        <div class="rv">
          <Photo src="dc-elevation.jpg" alt="Stacked-stone piers and a curved stucco wall at the entrance to a custom desert home" />
        </div>
        <div class="rv rv-d1">
          <p class="eyebrow">Building here</p>
          <h2 class="display h-md" style="margin-bottom:24px">The hillside ordinance decides more than the architect does.</h2>
          <p class="lede">The Foothills is unincorporated Pima County, not City of Tucson, and that single fact changes the whole job. Permits go through Pima County, and most of the good lots fall under the hillside development standards: slope limits, protected peaks and ridges, restrictions on how much of the natural terrain you are allowed to disturb, and color and reflectivity rules on everything you can see from below.</p>
          <p class="lede">Builders who work these lots occasionally treat the ordinance as an obstacle to be argued with. We treat it as the first design constraint. It is the difference between a house that reads as part of the slope and one that looks like it landed there.</p>
          <p class="lede">One Foothills client put it more plainly than we would: the house came in on time and on budget under that ordinance, and passed every inspection on the first try.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= WHAT IT TAKES ================= -->
  <section class="section section--warm">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid-head rv">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What a Foothills build asks for</p>
          <h2 class="display h-lg">Three things worth getting right.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="svc">
        <div class="svc__i rv">
          <div class="svc__n">01</div>
          <h3>Slope and access</h3>
          <p>Steep ground drives the cost long before the finishes do. Retaining, over-excavation, how a concrete truck physically reaches the pour, where the crane sets up. All of it is decided by the driveway, and the driveway is decided by the slope.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="svc__i rv rv-d1">
          <div class="svc__n">02</div>
          <h3>Washes and drainage</h3>
          <p>Foothills lots shed water fast and in specific places. Getting the drainage right protects the house, the neighbours downhill and the permit. Getting it wrong is the most expensive correction on this kind of site.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="svc__i rv rv-d2">
          <div class="svc__n">03</div>
          <h3>The view from below</h3>
          <p>The County cares what the house looks like from the valley floor: muted colors, limited reflectivity, restraint on the ridgeline. Designing to that from day one is what keeps the review short.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= FACTS ================= -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--top">
        <div class="rv">
          <p class="eyebrow">The practical details</p>
          <h2 class="display h-md" style="margin-bottom:28px">Working in the Foothills.</h2>
          <p class="lede">We are a licensed Arizona general contractor working throughout Pima County, with decades of hillside work behind us. If you are weighing two lots, we will walk both with you before you commit to either.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rv rv-d1">
          <dl class="deflist">
            <div><dt>Jurisdiction</dt><dd>Unincorporated Pima County. County permitting, not City of Tucson</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Areas</dt><dd>Ventana Canyon, Skyline, Pima Canyon, Finger Rock, Sabino Canyon, La Paloma</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>Steep slope, rock outcrop and wash crossings</dd></div>
            <div><dt>We build</dt><dd>Custom homes, whole-home remodels, additions, guest houses, pools and outdoor living</dd></div>
            <div><dt>License</dt><dd>Arizona ROC #324057. General Dual, active</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Telephone</dt><dd><a href="tel:+15209750456">(520) 975-0456</a></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= TESTIMONIAL ================= -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="quote rv">
        <hr class="rule rule--center">
        <blockquote>&ldquo;Our home was completed ON TIME and on BUDGET, despite falling under the County's onerous and restrictive hillside ordinance &hellip; The house passed every inspection on the FIRST try.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <cite>Homeowner &middot; Custom home client</cite>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= CTA ================= -->
  <section class="cta">
    <div class="cta__media"><Photo src="dc-walk-dusk.jpg" alt="" /></div>
    <div class="cta__inner rv">
      <h2 class="display h-lg">Building in the Foothills?</h2>
      <p>Send us the parcel number and the scope. We will tell you honestly what the site is going to ask of the budget.</p>
      <div class="cta__btns">
        <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact.html">Start a conversation</a>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href="tel:+15209750456">(520) 975-0456</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
